A.8 Extended Kalman Filter Derivation

For the nonlinear system $\mathbf{x}_{k+1} = f(\mathbf{x}_k,\mathbf{u}_k) + \mathbf{w}_k$, $\mathbf{z}_k = h(\mathbf{x}_k) + \mathbf{v}_k$, the EKF linearises about the current estimate. The prediction step:

\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k-1} = f(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k-1|k-1}, \mathbf{u}_k)


\mathbf{P}_{k|k-1} = \mathbf{F}_k \mathbf{P}_{k-1|k-1} \mathbf{F}_k^T + \mathbf{Q}_k, \quad \mathbf{F}_k = \left.\frac{\partial f}{\partial \mathbf{x}}\right|_{\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k-1|k-1}}

The update step uses the measurement residual $\mathbf{y}_k = \mathbf{z}_k - h(\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k-1})$ and innovation covariance $\mathbf{S}_k = \mathbf{H}_k \mathbf{P}_{k|k-1} \mathbf{H}_k^T + \mathbf{R}_k$ with $\mathbf{H}_k = \partial h/\partial \mathbf{x}|_{\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k-1}}$. The Kalman gain is $\mathbf{K}_k = \mathbf{P}_{k|k-1} \mathbf{H}_k^T \mathbf{S}_k^{-1}$. Then

\hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k} = \hat{\mathbf{x}}_{k|k-1} + \mathbf{K}_k \mathbf{y}_k


\mathbf{P}_{k|k} = (\mathbf{I} - \mathbf{K}_k \mathbf{H}_k) \mathbf{P}_{k|k-1}

Under Gaussian noise, this is the best linear unbiased estimator. Consistency (estimator errors bounded by covariance) is monitored via the normalised innovation squared (NIS) test: $NIS_k = \mathbf{y}_k^T \mathbf{S}_k^{-1} \mathbf{y}_k \sim \chi^2(m)$. If $NIS_k$ exceeds the 95% threshold, the process noise $\mathbf{Q}_k$ is inflated to account for unmodelled dynamics.

